@startuml INA700_application
' INA700 - application layer
' Author: Suraj Karki
' Course: INA700 - AI-based pick and place
'
' The use cases. They orchestrate the ports and hold no I/O of their own.

title INA700 - application layer

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #333333
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BackgroundColor<<port>> #EAF2FB
}

class VisionPipeline {
  -budget_ms : float
  +warm_up()
  +process(frame) : InferenceResult
}

class CoordinateService {
  -pick_depth_mm : float
  -angle_sign : int
  -slot_angles : Map<Shape, float>
  +to_pose(detection) : WorldPose
  +to_objects(detections) : List<DetectedObject>
}

class CycleController {
  -max_attempts : int
  -verify_tolerance_mm : float
  -cycle_index : int
  +run_cycle(request) : CycleReport
  -_object_was_lifted(target) : bool
}

class SharedState {
  -lock : RLock
  -snapshot : StateSnapshot
  +snapshot() : StateSnapshot
  +set_connected(connected)
  +set_inference_time(ms)
  +set_detections(objects)
  +set_status(text)
  +record_cycle(report)
}

interface ObjectSelector <<port>> {
  +{abstract} select(objects, request)
}

class AllowedShapeSelector
class ShapeRequestSelector
class ColourRequestSelector
class ConfidenceSelector
class OrientationConfidenceSelector {
  -minimum : float
}
class NearestToOriginSorter
class CompositeSelector {
  -selectors : List<ObjectSelector>
  +select(objects, request)
}

AllowedShapeSelector ..|> ObjectSelector
ShapeRequestSelector ..|> ObjectSelector
ColourRequestSelector ..|> ObjectSelector
ConfidenceSelector ..|> ObjectSelector
OrientationConfidenceSelector ..|> ObjectSelector
NearestToOriginSorter ..|> ObjectSelector
CompositeSelector ..|> ObjectSelector
CompositeSelector o-- "1..*" ObjectSelector : chains

CycleController --> CoordinateService
CycleController --> ObjectSelector
CycleController --> SharedState
VisionPipeline ..> CoordinateService : "InferenceResult"

note left of OrientationConfidenceSelector
  Drops an object whose angle could not be
  measured well enough to place on, rather
  than letting the estimator's honest 0 be
  mistaken for "sitting at zero degrees".
  Shape.is_rotationally_free exempts the
  circle, which has no angle to get wrong.
end note

note right of CompositeSelector
  Composite pattern. A new rule is a new class
  appended to the chain in the container;
  CycleController is never edited.
  Open for extension, closed for modification.
end note

note bottom of CycleController
  The robot has no grip sensor, so the CAMERA
  verifies: if an object of the same shape is
  still within verify_tolerance_mm of the
  commanded spot, the cup never lifted it and
  the cycle retries.
end note

' Hidden edges stack the selector chain into a column; side by side they make
' the diagram eight times wider than it is tall.
AllowedShapeSelector -[hidden]down- ConfidenceSelector
ConfidenceSelector -[hidden]down- OrientationConfidenceSelector
OrientationConfidenceSelector -[hidden]down- ShapeRequestSelector
ShapeRequestSelector -[hidden]down- ColourRequestSelector
ColourRequestSelector -[hidden]down- NearestToOriginSorter

@enduml
